diff --git a/docs/research.md b/docs/research.md
index fd1e4c7..fa62c4e 100644
--- a/docs/research.md
+++ b/docs/research.md
@@ -91,6 +91,11 @@ Practical consequences:
 - **Use `--repeats`.** Repeats reduce per-task noise but do not multiply your
   sample size; five attempts on 40 tasks is not 200 independent observations.
   Groundhog collapses repeats by majority vote for exactly this reason.
+- **`--jobs N` buys back the wall clock.** Repeats multiply the length of a run,
+  not its cost per attempt. Each attempt gets its own git worktree and its own
+  temporary tree, so running several at once produces the same records --
+  they simply land in `--out` out of order. Pick N from what your test suite and
+  your provider's rate limit will take, not from your core count.
 - **Report intervals, not point estimates.** `compare` prints Wilson intervals.
   A benchmark number without one invites over-reading.
 
